<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Llobregat</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Llobregat River</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Llobregat is a river in Catalonia, north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, about 170 km long. It rises in the Pre-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a> near Castellar de n'Hug, flows south through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bergueda">Berguedà</a> and past Montserrat, and enters the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> in a delta just south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a>, where the city's port and airport now stand. Its valley was a corridor of textile mills in the 19th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/llobregat.jpg" alt="Llobregat" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David.gaya · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Llobregat_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
